First-grab zero check + never-used free-page scanner + poison-on-free +
ptd node checks: the split experiment for the stray-writer hunt.

The shim scrubs [topOfKernelData, window end) to zero before entry, so a
managed page must read all-zero until it is handed out. sweet_fg_bits[]
marks pages that have ever left the free pool; every handout (all four
vm_page_grab_options returns via SWEET_CHECK_HANDOUT, cpm_allocate's
contiguous lists, and pmap_next_page_hi bootstrap steals) civacs + scans
a first-grab page and panics with PA + offset + first bad qwords on a
nonzero word.

Freed previously-used pages get a self-describing poison pattern
(0xf2ee<<48 | ppnum<<16 | qword index) written at BOTH free-queue
enqueue sites (vm_page_release and the vm_page_free_list batch path);
a separate sweet_pz_bits[] "is poisoned now" bit is set on each poison
write and cleared on each grab, so a freed page that bypassed a
poisoning enqueue can never produce a false used-freed hit. Side
effect: poison found inside a live object in a later dump proves a
double-free/double-ownership path, and the embedded ppnum names the
page.

A kernel thread (started at kernel_bootstrap_thread and again from
sweet_ufs_init, idempotent) sweeps free-queue pages at 1024 pages per
~100 ms tick plus one full pass at start (civac to PoC first, so a
non-coherent writer cannot hide behind stale cached zeros), checking
zero-fill for never-used pages and poison for used-then-freed ones;
hits log PA + offset + q_state + queue color + mach_absolute_time, and
the first 4 hits plus every ZCHECK panic are persisted through
sweet_ufs_diag_write (sweet_ufs_lock held when not panicking - the
record write shares the bounce buffer with live strategy I/O).

ptd pops additionally validate every next_node word (NULL or
8-aligned kernel VA) before it can reach the head, and the
reserve-page walk branch re-verifies the new head node's word: either
fires one step before a wild ptd_free_list head forms, with the node's
VA, PA, count and bad word (the pages are bzero'd by
pmap_pages_alloc_zeroed after the first-grab window, which ZCHECK
alone cannot see).

Boot args: sweetzcheck=0 (first-grab off), sweetscan=0 (scanner off,
default 1 report, 2 panic on hit), sweetscan_n=N (pages/tick, def
1024), sweetpoison=0 (poison-on-free off). The fill= boot arg
legitimately patterns free pages, so the checks stand down when set.

